    "https://jobs.careerbeacon.com/details/administrative-assistant-to-the-deans/2239837?utm_source=St.+Thomas+University&utm_medium=widget&utm_campaign=refer&utm_content=2239837&utm_term=jobtitle": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant to the Deans",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant to the Deans at St. Thomas University | Careerbeacon.com St. Thomas University Administrative Assistant to the Deans Fredericton, NB Apply Later Apply Now Discover The Opportunity Fredericton, NB Administrative Experienced Full-time $46,206 - $63,695 / year Benefits: Health Insurance Dental Insurance Paid Time Off Pension plan Group RRSP Retirement Plans Life Insurance Employee Assistance Program Wellness Programs Reporting to the Dean of Humanities and the Dean of Social Sciences, the Administrative Assistant provides essential administrative and clerical support by ensuring that the informational, organizational and communication needs of the Deans are met in a timely manner through the effective prioritization of activities and workflow. The position interacts regularly with a diverse array of constituents including staff, faculty, students, and various external stakeholders. Term: Permanent Hours of work: Full-Time (35 hours per week); Monday to Friday; 8:30 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Classification/Level: B2, Exempt Salary Range: $46,206 - $63,695 Closing Date: Monday, September 21, 2026 Share What you'll do Responsibilities Given the nature of the Office of the Dean of Humanities and the Dean of Social Sciences, the Administrative Assistant functions independently at times and is expected to exercise good judgment on issues, questions, and problems that arise. The incumbent must have the ability to follow through independently so that tasks and processes are completed in the prescribed timeline. Routinely has access to information of a confidential and sensitive nature and must be able to recognize the sensitivity of issues and maintain strict confidentiality. Manages the schedule of appointments and meetings for the Deans and resolves scheduling conflicts on a routine basis by identifying high priority requests. The incumbent manages telephone, mail, email, and in-person inquiries on the Deans' behalf, and coordinates arrangements for meetings, travel, and conferences. Frequently drafts correspondence and assists with the preparation and drafting of reports, and otherwise relieves the Deans of a variety of office and administrative details. Access to and possesses information relating to employer/employee relations, bargaining, employee, and student grievances, etc. The incumbent must have a working knowledge of the full and part-time collective agreements, university policies, and organizational structure of the University and have the ability to accurately interpret same. Assists the Deans by gathering required information for the preparation of reports to various committees and is frequently called upon for proofreading of reports, letters, and other printed material, necessitating knowledge of proper grammar, spelling, punctuation, and vocabulary. Works with the HR department on matters relating to part-time academic hiring, contracts, seniority, etc. Issues and monitors academic contracts and distributes signed copies to appropriate internal departments and FAUST. Works with the ITS department to update and modernize (when necessary) the electronic timetable site and reviews information with the Deans once the site has been closed before sending to the Registrar. Provides training for those using the system. Serves as the initial point of contact with individuals from both inside and outside the University, including senior administrators, faculty, staff, students, and government officials. Not infrequently, determines whether these people should more appropriately see someone other than the Deans and will direct them accordingly. In carrying out these functions, as well as others, the incumbent must maintain professionalism and, in many cases, strict confidentiality. Serves as the point person/contact for faculty and Access Copyright; submits confirmation forms, tracks, and processes the associated costs and fees and fields questions regarding copying on campus. Receives information on academic-related student travel, checks and follows up on information, advises on processes, monitors deadlines, and advises applicants on approvals. Assists in the organization of various special projects; e.g., Deans' List Dinner/Reception; Commencement Ceremony, Academic Orientation Day, and Mature/Transfer Student Reception. Maintains filing systems and databases. Enters, manipulates, and retrieves computer data to compile statistics and other information as requests in preparing specialized reports, including the use of Informer reports. Prepares letters and spreadsheets for distribution to Department Chairs/Programme Directors and Administrative Units. Performs other related duties as required. What you'll need Qualifications Post-secondary diploma or degree, Community College degree, or recognized Business School degree combined with a minimum of five years of experienc in a professional, automated office environment, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Ability to function independently and to exercise good judgment. Ability to recognize the sensitivity of issues and maintain strict confidentiality. Extensive knowledge of collective agreements, university policy, and organizational structure of a university or college would be an asset. Ability to organize and complete work assignments in a busy office environment. Experience using a variety of software applications, including Microsoft Office 365 products, Teams, and Colleague. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. WORKING CONDITIONS: Regular requirement to work under pressure to meet deadlines. Awareness of a variety of activities which are proceeding simultaneously. Conflicting demands may cause stress. Closing date: Monday, September 21, 2026. Candidates are responsible for clearly demonstrating in their cover letters how they meet the requirements of the position. All applications are to be received by 4:00 p.m. on the closing date. Please email your cover letter and resume to Human Resources ( [email protected] ). Please note that the selection process may include testing related to the advertised requirements. Candidates will be advised of any testing prior to the interview. An equal opportunity employer, St. Thomas University is committed to employment equity for women, Aboriginal peoples, members of visible minority groups, and persons with disabilities. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given priority. Candidates must have proof they are legally entitled to work in Canada. St. Thomas University is situated on the traditional territory of the Wolastoqiyik, Wəlastəkewiyik / Maliseet whose ancestors along with the Mi'Kmaq / Mi'kmaw and Passamaquoddy / Peskotomuhkati Tribes / Nations signed Peace and Friendship Treaties with the British Crown in the 1700s. © 2023 St. Thomas University. Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada. We're looking for Core Skills Interpersonal and Communication Microsoft Office Strong organizational skills Knowledge of University Organizational Structure Knowledge of University Policy Knowledge of collective agreements High Level Of Confidentiality Independence Office Administration Look for yourself Photo Gallery A little bit about us St. Thomas University St. Thomas University Founded in 1910, St. Thomas is a primarily undergraduate university located in Fredericton, NB. With an enrolment of 1,700 students, STU offers Bachelor of Arts and Bachelor of Social Work degrees for undergraduates, in addition to distinctive program opportunities like the Bachelor of Arts (Aviation Stream), the Mi’kmaq and Wolastoqey Bachelor of Social Work, and the Bachelor of Applied Arts. For those interested in post-degree or graduate studies, St. Thomas offers a Bachelor of Education and a Master of Social Work. Professors are distinguished scholars, authors, and commentators, and provide an outstanding education to their students. STU outperforms the Canadian university average for effective teaching, a supportive environment, student-faculty interactions, and higher order learning (National Survey of Student Engagement). Students report greater gains in critical thinking, writing, and problem solving when compared to the national average (CUSC Survey of First-Year Students). The university holds Canada Research Chairs in global and transnational studies and in physical culture and social life, as well as a health research chair in community health and aging. Mission St. Thomas University prioritizes teaching and learning so that each student is prepared for personal and career fulfillment. Through leading programs informed by our humanistic approach and opportunities for experiential education, we offer a robust and inclusive learning community that fosters connections across academic disciplines and emerging scholarly areas. On our beautiful campus, supportive faculty and staff create the ideal place for discovery and possibility. Each St. Thomas student is empowered to think independently, communicate effectively, and act responsibly. Meaningful contributions to the communities we serve locally, nationally, and globally are made today, through our teaching and research, and tomorrow, through the success of our alumni. Vision St. Thomas University commits to become the leading choice for students seeking a holistic university student experience. Apply Now View Careers Page Powered by Apply Later Enter your email to receive a reminder to apply for this position at a later date. * Email Apply Later We will send you an email reminder to with a link to this job. Cancel Create Reminder"
    },
    "https://jobs.careerbeacon.com/apply/2239837?utm_source=St.+Thomas+University&utm_medium=widget&utm_campaign=refer&utm_content=2239837&utm_term=apply": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant to the Deans",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant to the Deans | careerbeacon.com Administrative Assistant to the Deans St. Thomas University | Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada View job description Application Questions Review How would you like to start? Select one of our quick apply options. Import Resume Previous Application Apply Manually Loading... Import Options Contact Information Education Add your educational experience below. Add Education Work Experience Describe all related work experience below. Add Experience Languages Add the languages you are fluent in. Language Core Skills Select the core skills you possess that make you a great fit for this job. Additional Skills (Optional) Add any additional skills you possess that you feel are related to this position. Add Online Presence (Optional) If you are interested, you can share your online presence with the employer. Choose... LinkedIn Facebook Twitter Google+ Tumblr Dribbble GitHub Bitbucket AngelList YouTube Instagram Medium Reddit Vimeo Pinterest Flickr Other Website Add URL Highlights (Optional) Describe your most marketable strengths and talents. Limit to 600 characters. * Cover Letter Choose an option below. Both choices are valued equally. Write Cover Letter Attach Cover Letter Cover Letter Options * Resume/CV Attach Resume/CV Attachments (Optional) Attach documents that support your application (i.e., transcript or portfolio work) Upload Document Save and Continue Assistant Welcome to your job application! Remember always to put your best foot forward. Be as thorough as possible in the information you provide. Need clarification on something? Just check out the tips I offer you along the way. Tips Contact Information Education Work Experience Languages Core Skills Additional Skills Online Presence Highlights Cover Letter Resume/CV Contact Information I admit this is pretty self-explanatory. But, I do want to remind you to double check your phone number and email address. A tiny mistake could have big implications! Return to tips Education This is where you add all relevant education experience you wish to share. In the description, be sure to add what courses you excelled in and what projects you completed which were really cool. Return to tips Work Experience It’s necessary to share work experience related to the job you are applying for. In the description, be sure to highlight what your major accomplishments were in each previous role. This gives the employer insight into what your responsibilities were and what you are capable of. Use this section to detail any relevant volunteer experience as well. Return to tips Languages Pretty simple. Just select the languages in which you have a working proficiency. Easy peasy. Return to tips Core Skills Mindfully select the skills that help you perform at your best. Core skills are a way for employers to understand you so they can make informed decisions. So be honest ;) Return to tips Additional Skills Have more skills to share? Do it here! Return to tips Online Presence Perhaps you have a stellar blog or a great LinkedIn profile. Share the links here for the employer to explore. Return to tips Highlights The Highlights section appears at the very top of your application. It’s pretty important, so make it count! Highlight key achievements, mention things that stand out about you as a person and your experiences, and if you can, give them a bit of insight into your personality. Help them remember you. You’re amazing, so tell them. Return to tips Cover Letter If you choose Write Cover Letter, you can write it right here in the application. Or you can attach your cover letter (PDF recommended). Return to tips Resume/CV Here you can attach your resume. Attaching your resume here will not overwrite any other info you’ve already imported. We recommend you upload your resume as a PDF file. File types: .pdf,.docx,.doc,.rtf,.txt,.odt Maximum file size is 20 MB. Return to tips Attachments Some employers want to see more. Be sure to check the application to see if they request any additional documentation. Maximum file size is 20 MB. Return to tips Sorry, but it looks like you've missed something. Return to tips Need more help? Uploading file, please wait... Cancel upload × Error: The resume uploaded couldn't be imported properly. Our system only accepts certain file types (.doc, .docx, .pdf for example). If you can convert your file to one of these file types, we should be able to import all of your information. If you experience any issues, you can email us at [email protected] . Close Window Log in to your Alongside Account Wrong Username/Email and password combination. Sorry, but it looks like you've already applied for this position. Email address (success) Password (success) Login Forgot Password? SOCIAL LOGIN Login with Facebook Login with LinkedIn Login with Google Close Which profile would you like to use? Sorry, but it looks like you've already applied for this position. Default \n                                  | Last applied position: None"
